I fixed the bug. All 38 vitest test files (281 tests) pass and `npx tsc --noEmit` is clean.

**Cause:** Coaching replies are read by `prepareJsonString` in `lib/claude-json.ts`. Before parsing, it turned every raw newline and tab into the two-character text `\n` or `\t`, so that line breaks inside text values wouldn't break the parser. But it also did this to the line breaks and indentation *between* fields. When the model sent its reply spread over several lines, which is common for long replies, the result had stray `\n` text right after the opening `{`. The parser rejected that, and the app showed "could not read the reply." Replies that happened to come back on one line worked, which is why the same request sometimes succeeded.

**Fix:** I replaced the blanket replace with a small scanner that tracks whether it is inside a quoted text value. It escapes raw newlines, carriage returns and tabs only inside those values, and leaves the whitespace between fields alone. It handles escaped quotes and backslashes correctly. Removing other stray control characters works as before. Both coaching routes in `app/api/coach/reflect/route.ts` go through this function, so they get the fix.

**Test:** I added `lib/claude-json.multiline.test.ts`. It covers a long, indented reply wrapped in a code block, with tab indentation, Windows-style line endings, a line break inside a text value, and escaped quotes and backslashes. The existing tests for multi-line JSON, which were the ones failing before, now pass too.

One thing I left alone: the function still finds the end of the reply by looking for the last `}`. Extra text after the reply that contains a `}` will still break parsing. I kept that because an existing test checks for this behaviour and I'm not allowed to change it.
AGENT_RC=0
